<%# THE ONE USER THIS PAGE HAS NOTHING TO DRAW: no expense category at all.

    ** THE GATE MOVED FROM "no rules" TO "no categories" (two-shapes spec §4). ** The list is every
    expense category now, so a user with three categories and no rules is not empty — they have
    three rows, each with a "+ New rule for <category>" button inside it, which is exactly the
    screen this frame used to stand in for. What is left is the user with nowhere to put a rule, and
    the honest thing to offer them is a category.

    A frame rather than a blank page: an empty screen reads as something that failed to load. %>
<section class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded px-6 py-8 text-center" data-budget-empty>
  <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">No spending categories yet</h3>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500 max-w-xl mx-auto">
    A rule claims part of every period's income for one category, so a category comes first — make
    one and it appears here, in the order they give way.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4">
    <%= link_to "Add a category", new_category_path, class: "btn btn-primary" %>
  </p>
</section>
